// Conway's Game of Life — matrix edition.
//
// Everything lives inside the collections book's scope: the board is a
// matrix (rectangular by construction), dimensions come from the rows /
// columns of it, and cells are read and written with item at (r, c).
// Edges wrap.

Pull a book on collections.

Bind number to wrap-index, given (the number i, the number extent):
    If i is less than 1, return i + extent.
    If i is greater than extent, return i - extent.
    Return i.
Done.

Bind matrix to make-board, given (the number height, the number width):
    Return a matrix with height by width filled with 0.
Done.

Bind void to set-cell, given (the matrix board, the number r, the number c):
    Define height as the rows of board.
    Define width as the columns of board.
    Define rr as cast wrap-index on (r, height).
    Define cc as cast wrap-index on (c, width).
    The item at (rr, cc) of board becomes 1.
Done.

// Stamp a text pattern ("#" = alive) with its top-left corner at (top, left).
Bind void to stamp, given (the matrix board, the series of text pattern,
                           the number top, the number left):
    Define pr as 0.
    For each line in pattern, repeat:
        Define line-len as the length of line.
        Define pc as 1.
        While pc is less than line-len + 1, repeat:
            Define ch as the characters from pc to pc of line.
            If ch is "#":
                Cast set-cell on (board, top + pr, left + pc - 1).
            Done.
            The pc becomes pc + 1.
        Done.
        The pr becomes pr + 1.
    Done.
Done.

Bind number to count-neighbors, given (the matrix board, the number r, the number c):
    Define height as the rows of board.
    Define width as the columns of board.
    Define total as 0.
    For each dr in range 0 - 1 to 1, repeat:
        For each dc in range 0 - 1 to 1, repeat:
            If dr is 0 and dc is 0, skip.
            Define rr as cast wrap-index on (r + dr, height).
            Define cc as cast wrap-index on (c + dc, width).
            Define v as item at (rr, cc) of board.
            The total becomes total + v.
        Done.
    Done.
    Return total.
Done.

Bind matrix to next-board, given (the matrix board):
    Define height as the rows of board.
    Define width as the columns of board.
    Define next as cast make-board on (height, width).
    For each r in range 1 to height, repeat:
        For each c in range 1 to width, repeat:
            Define alive as item at (r, c) of board.
            Define n as cast count-neighbors on (board, r, c).
            If alive is 1:
                If n is 2 or n is 3:
                    The item at (r, c) of next becomes 1.
                Done.
            Done.
            Otherwise:
                If n is 3:
                    The item at (r, c) of next becomes 1.
                Done.
            Done.
        Done.
    Done.
    Return next.
Done.

Bind void to render, given (the matrix board):
    Define height as the rows of board.
    Define width as the columns of board.
    For each r in range 1 to height, repeat:
        Define line as "".
        For each c in range 1 to width, repeat:
            Define cell as item at (r, c) of board.
            If cell is 1:
                The line becomes line joined to "#".
            Done.
            Otherwise:
                The line becomes line joined to ".".
            Done.
        Done.
        State line.
    Done.
Done.

Bind void to play:
    Define board as cast make-board on (16, 32).

    Define glider as a series of text with (
        ".#.",
        "..#",
        "###").

    Define pulsar as a series of text with (
        "..###...###..",
        ".............",
        "#....#.#....#",
        "#....#.#....#",
        "#....#.#....#",
        "..###...###..",
        ".............",
        "..###...###..",
        "#....#.#....#",
        "#....#.#....#",
        "#....#.#....#",
        ".............",
        "..###...###..").

    Cast stamp on (board, pulsar, 2, 2).
    Cast stamp on (board, glider, 2, 20).
    Cast stamp on (board, glider, 12, 28).

    Define gens as 24.
    Define g as 0.
    While g is less than gens, repeat:
        State "Generation " joined to g converted to text.
        Cast render on (board).
        State "".
        The board becomes cast next-board on (board).
        The g becomes g + 1.
    Done.
Done.

Cast play.

Done.